            <ArticleTitle>[Clinical findings in thoracal functional disturbances (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>755-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Functional disorders of the thoracal motor structures show connections with visceral functions through the different forms of pain symptoms, but also not seldom without these, or else appear as their precursors. By means of conventional examination parameters, corresponding interconnection procedures could be demonstrated and the theoretical models for further discussion of the segmental reflector complexes are substantiated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
